### Minimal Fixes

1. **Add `DeactivateAsync` to `UserService`**

   ```csharp
   // UserService.cs
   using Api.Models;
   using Api.Repositories;

   namespace Api.Services;

   public class UserService
   {
       private readonly UserRepository _repo;

       public UserService(UserRepository repo)
       {
           _repo = repo;
       }

       // Existing methods...

       /// <summary>
       /// Deactivates a user by setting the Active flag to false.
       /// </summary>
       /// <param name="userId">The ID of the user to deactivate.</param>
       /// <returns>A task representing the asynchronous operation.</returns>
       /// <exception cref="KeyNotFoundException">Thrown if the user does not exist.</exception>
       public async Task DeactivateAsync(int userId)
       {
           // Attempt to retrieve the user first
           var user = await _repo.GetUserByIdAsync(userId);
           if (user == null)
           {
               throw new KeyNotFoundException($"User {userId} not found");
           }

           // If the user is already inactive, no-op
           if (!user.Active)
           {
               return;
           }

           // Update the flag
           user.Active = false;

           // Persist the change
           await _repo.UpdateAsync(user);
       }
   }
   ```

   *Assumptions*  
   * `UserRepository` exposes `GetUserByIdAsync(int)` and `UpdateAsync(User)` (or a similarly named method).  
   * The `User` model contains an `Active` boolean property.

2. **Optional Performance Improvement**

   If the repository already has a method that updates only the `Active` column (e.g., `SetActiveAsync(int userId, bool active)`), replace the two‑step fetch‑update with a single call:

   ```csharp
   public async Task DeactivateAsync(int userId)
   {
       // Directly set the flag; repository handles existence check
       var success = await _repo.SetActiveAsync(userId, false);
       if (!success)
       {
           throw new KeyNotFoundException($"User {userId} not found");
       }
   }
   ```

   This eliminates an extra round‑trip.

